  <static seed="1933" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers60.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p>Do not use a calculator.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{1} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{0.01} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{0.0001} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.01</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>First, recognize that <m>1</m> is a square number. Since <m>1\cdot1=1</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{1}=1</m>.</p>
<p>Next, since <m>0.1\cdot0.1=0.01</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{0.01}=0.1</m>.</p>
<p>Finally, since <m>0.01\cdot0.01=0.0001</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{0.0001}=0.01</m>.</p>
</solution>
